  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607195600: Purpose-bound non-exporting SCRAM secret capability

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

PostgreSQL password material must not be read into component memory. The
native boundary exposes `scram_sha256`, guarded by the capability
`secret/use-scram-sha256`. A component supplies an opaque credential reference,
server salt, bounded iteration count and SCRAM authentication transcript. The
host requires an exact reference in both the capability allowlist and injected
credential store, then returns only the 32-byte client proof followed by the
32-byte expected server signature.

The operation is default-denied, requires secret and write opt-in, and has a
call-time proof quota. Salt, iteration and transcript bounds are checked before
PBKDF2/HMAC. The `.kotoba` provider component contains no password and cannot
request a generic secret export.

## Maturity boundary

The cryptographic seam is verified through real Wasm against a fixed
SCRAM-SHA-256 vector. PostgreSQL AuthenticationSASL message parsing, nonce
generation, SASL framing and server-final verification are not yet implemented
and therefore password-authenticated `pg-open` is not yet qualified.")))
